VALUES
('La Llorona', 'Mexico City', 'Mexico', 1940, 'A weeping woman who drowns her children and now cries for them near bodies of water.', 'Weeping woman in white', 0.85, 'oral', '2022-05-15', 19.4326, -99.1332, 8.50, 150234, 'Folklore Archives', 'https://evidence.net/llorona.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/llorona.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 10:00:00'),
('The Vanishing Hitchhiker', 'Various', 'USA', 1930, 'A young woman is picked up while hitchhiking, gives an address, and then vanishes from the car. The driver later learns she died years ago.', 'Ghostly young woman', 0.70, 'oral', '2021-10-31', 34.0522, -118.2437, 7.20, 89456, 'Urban Legend Compendium', 'https://evidence.net/hitchhiker.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/hitchhiker.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 11:00:00'),
('Bloody Mary', 'Toledo', 'USA', 1978, 'A spirit or witch who is said to appear in a mirror when her name is chanted multiple times.', 'Mirror-dwelling spirit', 0.60, 'oral', '2023-11-01', 41.6639, -83.5552, 9.10, 540192, 'Adolescent Folklore', 'https://evidence.net/mary.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/mary.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 12:00:00'),
('Chupacabra', 'Ponce', 'Puerto Rico', 1995, 'A creature that attacks and drinks the blood of livestock, especially goats.', 'Vampiric reptilian creature', 0.45, 'newspaper', '2023-01-20', 18.0111, -66.6145, 6.80, 210345, 'Cryptozoology Weekly', 'https://evidence.net/chupacabra.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/chupacabra.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 13:00:00'),
('Slender Man', 'Internet', 'Global', 2009, 'A tall, thin, faceless man in a black suit who stalks, abducts, or traumatizes people, particularly children.', 'Tall, faceless man', 0.95, 'internet forum', '2020-06-09', 34.0522, -118.2437, 9.80, 2304567, 'Something Awful Forums', 'https://evidence.net/slenderman.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/slenderman.jpg', true, '2024-01-01 14:00:00'),
('Mothman', 'Point Pleasant', 'USA', 1966, 'A large, winged humanoid creature with glowing red eyes, reportedly seen before a major bridge collapse.', 'Winged humanoid, red eyes', 0.55, 'newspaper', '1967-12-15', 38.8426, -82.1404, 6.50, 180432, 'Local Press Archives', 'https://evidence.net/mothman.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/mothman.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 15:00:00'),
('Alligators in the Sewers', 'New York City', 'USA', 1930, 'Pet baby alligators, flushed down toilets, are said to survive and thrive in city sewer systems.', 'Albino alligators', 0.30, 'oral', '1985-05-20', 40.7128, -74.0060, 5.50, 45098, 'Municipal Worker Tales', 'https://evidence.net/gator.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/gator.jpg', true, '2024-01-01 16:00:00'),
('The Russian Sleep Experiment', 'Internet', 'Global', 2010, 'A story about Soviet researchers in the late 1940s who used an experimental stimulant gas on political prisoners, who eventually became monstrous beings.', 'Mutated prisoners', 0.80, 'internet forum', '2010-08-10', 55.7558, 37.6173, 8.90, 950321, 'Creepypasta Wiki', 'https://evidence.net/sleep.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/sleep.jpg', true, '2024-01-01 17:00:00'),
('Polybius', 'Portland', 'USA', 1981, 'A fictitious 1981 arcade game that was part of a government-run psychology experiment, causing intense psychoactive and addictive effects.', 'Arcade cabinet', 0.65, 'internet forum', '1981-12-01', 45.5051, -122.6750, 7.50, 120876, 'Coin-op Enthusiasts', 'https://evidence.net/polybius.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/polybius.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 18:00:00'),
('Black-Eyed Children', 'Abilene', 'USA', 1996, 'Supernatural creatures that resemble children with pale skin and solid black eyes, who are reportedly seen hitchhiking or on doorsteps.', 'Children with black eyes', 0.75, 'newspaper', '2013-09-12', 32.4487, -99.7331, 8.20, 340987, 'Journalist Brian Bethel', 'https://evidence.net/bec.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/bec.jpg', false, '2024-01-01 19:00:00'),
('The Jersey Devil', 'Pine Barrens', 'USA', 1735, 'A demonic creature with hooves, a goat-like head, bat wings, and a forked tail, said to inhabit the Pine Barrens of Southern New Jersey.', 'Kangaroo-like creature with wings', 0.80, 'oral', '2009-01-19', 39.8360, -74.5395, 6.90, 95432, 'Local Folklore', 'https://evidence.net/jerseydevil.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/jerseydevil.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 09:00:00'),
('Teke Teke', 'Japan', 'Japan', 1960, 'The ghost of a young woman or schoolgirl who was cut in half by a train. She travels on her hands, making a scratching or ''teke teke'' sound.', 'Vengeful female ghost (upper torso)', 0.88, 'oral', '2004-08-21', 35.6895, 139.6917, 7.80, 112345, 'Japanese School Stories', 'https://evidence.net/teketeke.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/teketeke.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 10:00:00'),
('The Flying Dutchman', 'Cape of Good Hope', 'Global', 1790, 'A legendary ghost ship that can never make port and is doomed to sail the oceans forever. Its sighting is a portent of doom.', 'Ghostly ship and its captain', 0.90, 'oral', '1942-09-15', -34.3572, 18.4739, 8.10, 78901, 'Maritime Legends', 'https://evidence.net/dutchman.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/dutchman.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 11:00:00'),
('Kuchisake-onna (Slit-Mouthed Woman)', 'Japan', 'Japan', 1979, 'The malevolent spirit of a woman, mutilated by her husband, who returns as a vengeful ghost, covering her mouth and asking strangers if she is beautiful.', 'Woman with a mutilated mouth', 0.85, 'newspaper', '2007-11-28', 34.6937, 135.5023, 8.40, 134567, 'Gifu Prefecture Police Reports', 'https://evidence.net/kuchisake.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/kuchisake.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 12:00:00'),
('The Bell Witch', 'Adams', 'USA', 1817, 'A poltergeist haunting the Bell family. The entity was reportedly able to speak, affect the physical environment, and shapeshift.', 'Poltergeist, Kate Batts', 0.78, 'oral', '1821-03-01', 36.5806, -87.3542, 6.20, 65432, 'The Bell Family Chronicle', 'https://evidence.net/bellwitch.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/bellwitch.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 13:00:00'),
('Spring-heeled Jack', 'London', 'England', 1837, 'A figure in Victorian folklore with a terrifying appearance, who was said to be able to jump extraordinary heights.', 'Diabolical figure with claws', 0.72, 'newspaper', '1904-09-22', 51.5074, -0.1278, 6.80, 54321, 'Victorian Penny Dreadfuls', 'https://evidence.net/springheel.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/springheel.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 14:00:00'),
('The Beast of Gévaudan', 'Gévaudan', 'France', 1764, 'A man-eating wolf-like animal that terrorized the former province of Gévaudan. The attacks were so numerous that it was considered a national scourge.', 'Man-eating wolf or hybrid', 0.92, 'newspaper', '1767-06-19', 44.7031, 3.4994, 7.90, 87654, 'Historical Royal Decrees', 'https://evidence.net/gevaudan.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/gevaudan.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 15:00:00'),
('The Dybbuk Box', 'Portland', 'USA', 2001, 'A wine cabinet which is said to be haunted by a dybbuk, a restless, malicious spirit from Jewish folklore.', 'Haunted wine cabinet', 0.50, 'internet forum', '2004-02-14', 45.5051, -122.6750, 7.10, 145678, 'eBay Listing by Kevin Mannis', 'https://evidence.net/dybbuk.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/dybbuk.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 16:00:00'),
('The Manananggal', 'Visayas', 'Philippines', 1600, 'A mythical creature that can sever its upper torso and sprout huge bat-like wings to fly into the night in search of its victims.', 'Self-segmenting vampire', 0.87, 'oral', '2019-07-05', 10.7202, 123.4790, 7.60, 98765, 'Filipino Folklore', 'https://evidence.net/manananggal.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/manananggal.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 17:00:00'),
('The Green Children of Woolpit', 'Woolpit', 'England', 1150, 'Two children of unusual green skin color who reportedly appeared in the village of Woolpit, speaking an unknown language.', 'Two green-skinned children', 0.68, 'oral', '1152-01-01', 52.2198, 0.8897, 5.90, 43210, 'William of Newburgh Chronicles', 'https://evidence.net/greenchildren.mp3', 'https://evidence.net/greenchildren.jpg', false, '2024-02-01 18:00:00');
